# The harness's live server data directory. NEVER commit this.
#
# `start` creates a real t3 server instance here, which generates private
# signing keys, a state database, and a log containing pairing tokens and
# WebSocket tickets. An earlier commit swept the whole directory in via
# `git add tools/t3-server/` and tracked all of it. Review caught it.
#
# The glob is `.runtime*/`, not `.runtime/`. Spec 146 Phase 10 runs several
# servers at once — one per driver, plus the 24-hour gate — and `T3_HARNESS_DIR`
# gives each its own directory: `.runtime-claude-1h`, `.runtime-gate-24h`. Those
# hold the same signing keys and the same tokens, and the narrower pattern
# covered none of them.
.runtime*/
